WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.430
A guitar chord rings out, and its sound
wave rolls smoothly across the screen.

2
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.270
Now open the same song saved on a phone.

3
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.810
There's no wave in there.

4
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.090
Just a long column of numbers.

5
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.170
Press play, and that list of
numbers becomes the guitar again.

6
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.590
So how can a list of
numbers turn into a song?

7
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.770
In this mission, you'll
see that sound is analogue:

8
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.090
a wave that changes
smoothly and continuously.

9
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:30.970
You'll find out why that's a problem,
because a computer can only store binary.

10
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.450
And you'll meet amplitude:
the height of the wave.

11
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.640
Your mission: explain how a list
of numbers can turn into a song.
